   "name": "Southeast Buttress",
   "grade": "5.7",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "The Eichhorn pinnacle base is where the descent leads, staying high on climber's right over 3rd class with some exposure. Up the buttress, almost anywhere goes; its lowest middle point gives the most. A start higher and right loses vertical, with a poor first pitch. The lower three pitches grow harder (5.3 up to 5.6) and likely end in a chimney that jams with people and catches packs; left of it is smooth. Passing is easy for the competent.",
